## Prerequisites

- **cmake 3.25+** - Build system generator ([installation guide](https://cmake.org/download/))
- **ninja** - CMake generator used by all presets (`brew install ninja`)
- **conan 2.x** - C/C++ package manager for all third-party libraries (`brew install conan`)
- **C++{{cpp_standard}} compiler** - LLVM/Clang (`brew install llvm`; AppleClang is rejected)
- **just** - Command runner ([installation guide](https://github.com/casey/just#installation))
- **MoltenVK** (macOS only) - Vulkan driver/ICD (`brew install molten-vk`)

The following validation tools are also required:

| Tool | Purpose | Install |
|------|---------|---------|
| [clang-format](https://clang.llvm.org/docs/ClangFormat.html) | Code formatting | `brew install clang-format` |
| [clang-tidy](https://clang.llvm.org/extra/clang-tidy/) | Static analysis / linting | `brew install llvm` |
| [cppcheck](https://cppcheck.sourceforge.io/) | Static analysis | `brew install cppcheck` |
| [flawfinder](https://dwheeler.com/flawfinder/) | Security scanning | `brew install flawfinder` |
| [include-what-you-use](https://include-what-you-use.org/) | Include hygiene (advisory) | `brew install include-what-you-use` |
| [infer](https://github.com/facebook/infer) | Static analysis (null deref, memory leaks) | [releases](https://github.com/facebook/infer/releases) |
| [codespell](https://github.com/codespell-project/codespell) | Spell checking | `brew install codespell` |
| [semgrep](https://semgrep.dev/) | Custom static analysis | `brew install semgrep` |
| [lcov](https://github.com/linux-test-project/lcov) | Code coverage reporting | `brew install lcov` |

## Dependencies (Conan 2)

All third-party libraries are managed by Conan with exact version pins in
`conanfile.py` and installed by `just init` into `build/conan/<BuildType>/`.
The first `init` compiles every dependency from source for the local
LLVM/Clang toolchain (slow); afterwards the Conan cache makes it fast.

Included library stack:

| Domain | Libraries |
|--------|-----------|
| Windowing / input | SDL3 |
| Graphics (Vulkan) | vulkan-headers, vulkan-loader, volk, vk-bootstrap, VulkanMemoryAllocator, MoltenVK (macOS, via brew) |
| Shader toolchain | shaderc (bundles glslang), SPIRV-Tools, SPIRV-Cross |
| Math / ECS / physics | GLM, EnTT, Jolt Physics |
| Navigation / networking | Recast/Detour (recastnavigation), GameNetworkingSockets |
| Serialization | bitsery |
| Audio | Opus, miniaudio |
| Asset pipeline | tinygltf (glTF 2.0), meshoptimizer, KTX2/Basis Universal (libktx), ozz-animation, MikkTSpace |
| UI / tooling | Dear ImGui (docking), ImGuizmo, RmlUi, spdlog, fmt, Tracy |
| Data | SQLite3, libpqxx (PostgreSQL), zstd, xxHash |
| Testing | GoogleTest |

`gltfpack` (glTF optimizer CLI from the meshoptimizer project) is not
available through Conan; `just init` installs its prebuilt binary (pinned to
the meshoptimizer library version) into `~/.local/bin` on macOS, Linux, and
Windows (Git Bash/MSYS).

Every library has a smoke test in `tests/deps/` that proves it compiles,
links, and initializes headlessly — run them with `just test`.

### Adding a dependency

1. Add an exactly-pinned `self.requires("name/version")` to `conanfile.py`.
2. Add `find_package(...)` and the imported target to `target_link_libraries`
   in `CMakeLists.txt`.
3. Add a smoke test under `tests/deps/<name>_test.cpp`.
4. Run `just init && just test`.

## Setup

Initialize the project environment:

```bash
just init
```

This will:
- Check all prerequisite tools are installed
- Create the default Conan profile (if missing) and install all dependencies
  (Debug + Release; the first run compiles them from source)
- Configure the CMake debug preset
- Build the project

## Usage

Run the main application:

```bash
just run
```

Run the Vulkan cube demo — a visual end-to-end check that the graphics stack
(SDL3 window, Vulkan loader/driver, vk-bootstrap, shaderc, VMA, GLM, Dear
ImGui menu) actually works on this machine:

```bash
just demo                     # interactive: drag to rotate, Esc quits
just demo --auto-quit 5       # timed smoke run (used by CI-style checks)
```

See all available commands:

```bash
just help
```

Or simply:

```bash
just
```

## Development

### Available Commands

- `just init` - Initialize development environment
- `just run` - Run the main application
- `just demo` - Run the Vulkan cube demo (visual stack check)
- `just destroy` - Remove build artifacts
- `just help` - Show available commands

### Code Quality

- `just code-format` - Auto-fix code formatting (clang-format)
- `just code-style` - Check code style (clang-tidy)
- `just code-typecheck` - Run static analysis (cppcheck)
- `just code-security` - Run security checks (flawfinder)
- `just code-deptry` - Check include hygiene (IWYU, advisory)
- `just code-spell` - Check spelling
- `just code-semgrep` - Run custom static analysis

`just code-style` runs `clang-tidy` in quiet mode so CI output focuses on
diagnostics from project-owned source files. To inspect suppressed non-user,
system, or dependency warning context while debugging the clang-tidy setup,
remove `--quiet` from the `code-style` recipe in `justfile`.

### Testing

- `just test` - Run unit tests
- `just test-coverage` - Run tests with coverage ({{coverage_threshold}}% threshold)
- `just code-sanitize` - Run tests with AddressSanitizer + UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer

### CI

- `just ci` - Run all validation checks (verbose)
- `just ci-quiet` - Run all checks (silent, fail-fast)

The CI pipeline runs the following steps in order:
1. `init` - Initialize environment
2. `code-format` - Auto-format code
3. `code-style` - Check code style (clang-tidy)
4. `code-typecheck` - Static analysis (cppcheck)
5. `code-security` - Security scan (flawfinder)
6. `code-deptry` - Include hygiene (IWYU)
7. `code-spell` - Spell checking
8. `code-semgrep` - Custom static analysis
9. `test` - Unit tests
10. `code-sanitize` - Sanitizer tests

